[thin] The lead-in narrows toward the flat bearing at the end of each leaf. This continuous taper spreads the leaf over the ledge during assembly.
alternatives: Thickening the ramp would shorten the usable lead-in or widen the flat bearing. Both change entry and catch contact at the actual receiver.
